var e={"show.button":`Show me`,"show.badge":`New`,"show.done":`Got it`,"show.try":`Try it`,"show.gitBranchMenu.title":`Open a branch or a commit on GitHub with a right click`,"show.gitBranchMenu.body":`In a git graph - in the chat or on the Git page - right click a branch label or a commit (long press on a phone), then Open on GitHub: it opens on github.com in a new tab. Copy the GitHub link and copy the name / SHA are there too. What is not pushed yet says so.`,"show.msgActions.title":`Edit a stopped message, start a new session from any message`,"show.msgActions.body":`You stopped Claude too early? Click the pencil under your message (or right click → Edit): its text and attachments come back in the box, ready to fix and send. Right click any message - yours or a reply - then New session from this message: a new session of the same topic opens with it already typed (long press on Android).`,"show.fileMenu.title":`Right click on a file`,"show.fileMenu.body":`In a conversation, right click a picture, a video or a file path (long press on Android): open it, download it, copy its path, or quote it - your next message then carries its path on one line, and Claude opens the file only if it needs to.`,"show.videoQuality.title":`Video quality`,"show.videoQuality.body":`Big videos start fast: open one and pick Auto, Original, 1080p, 720p or 480p in the player (the button next to the speed). The server makes the lighter copy once, the video keeps playing meanwhile and switches at the same moment when it is ready. Auto plays a lighter copy only when the original is heavy (over 1080p, a high bitrate, or a format some browsers cannot play).`,"show.textZoom.title":`Your texts, at your size`,"show.textZoom.body":`In a .md or text file, "− 100% +" (or the T button when space is short) makes the text larger or smaller, also with Ctrl/⌘ + wheel. Harness remembers where you were: switching from Preview to Edit or opening the file again brings you back to the same passage.`,"show.look.title":`Your colors, everywhere`,"show.look.body":`The theme, accent and background you pick here now also color the sign-in page and any new browser (phone, private window).`,"show.infra.title":`Infra: everything you host, in one page`,"show.infra.body":`Turn on the Infra page here: every site, database, bucket, domain and server - this server, your other servers, Cloudflare, Hostinger - with its status and its links. Then just ask Claude "put this folder online" or "create a database for my app": it is done the standard way and shows up there.`,"show.infraServers.title":`Your other servers, in one click`,"show.infraServers.body":`A Hostinger VPS now connects by itself when it already accepts a key of this server, or with the Connect button: its sites and databases show up here. Any other server: Add a server. The Overview tab explains how the page works and what to do when a key or a right is missing.`,"show.pcBrowser.title":`Browser of my PC`,"show.pcBrowser.body":`Claude can use a browser on your own computer, in a separate profile: install Harness PC from here once. The browser opens only while Claude uses it.`,"show.mobileHeader.title":`A tidier header on phones`,"show.mobileHeader.body":`The top of a conversation now has three short lines: ☰, the app and ⊞; the session title; then the topic (tap it for its menu), the cost and a ring showing how full the context is. Menus and lists open from the bottom: slide them down to close.`,"show.touchNav.title":`A new layout for phones and tablets`,"show.touchNav.body":`The conversation now fills the screen. ☰ at the top left opens all your sessions (search, running, unread, projects); ⊞ at the top right opens everything else. Press and hold a session for its menu. On a computer nothing changes; Settings → General → Layout picks the layout of each device.`,"show.tasks.title":`Your tasks, project by project`,"show.tasks.body":`Every workspace project now has its tasks: pick it in the bar on the left, or open the Overview to see all your projects at once. Switch views at the top: Board (with one lane per project), Week - drag a task onto a day to give it that due date -, Calendar, or List by topic.`,"show.mcp.title":`The tools of Claude, at a glance`,"show.mcp.body":`Every MCP server (Google Ads, Notion, a database...) in one list: where it applies - every session or one topic - and whether it works. Add one, connect a service that needs a sign-in, or remove it. Claude can also do it for you: ask it in the topic.`,"show.infraDomains.title":`All your domains, wherever they are`,"show.infraDomains.body":`Every domain now shows its registrar, its expiry date, who serves its DNS and who hosts it - OVH, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Vercel, Netlify, Shopify... - without any key. Add any other domain here with Add a domain. Vercel, Netlify, Supabase and GitHub Pages can be connected too (Overview -> What Harness reads).`,"show.dashMotion.title":`A dashboard that builds itself`,"show.dashMotion.body":`Each card now assembles smoothly: numbers count up, lists rise in row by row, charts grow and draw, and Today’s schedule opens each job’s line and drops its runs on it from left to right. Cards lower on the page wait until you scroll to them, and the grid slides into place when the notifications panel opens.`,"show.git.title":`Git as a graph`,"show.git.body":`When Claude talks about a repository (branches, commits, what is not pushed), it now shows the real graph in the conversation. To see everything - the repositories of the server and your GitHub account with your rights - open the Git page (hide it in Settings -> Features if you like).`,"show.diagram.title":`Diagrams open like pictures`,"show.diagram.body":`Click a diagram in a conversation: it opens in the file viewer. The mouse wheel zooms by 5 % around the pointer, drag to move around, ← / → go through the other files of the conversation.`,"show.twofa.title":`Two-step sign-in with Telegram`,"show.twofa.body":`Turn it on here: after the password, every new browser waits for your approval in Telegram (Allow button or code). If Telegram ever stops answering, run maxxing 2fa off on the server.`,"show.idleCompact.title":`Back after a break: compact first`,"show.idleCompact.body":`Come back to a long session after more than an hour and its cache has expired: Harness now summarizes it before your message, so every following turn starts small instead of re-sending the whole history. Pick the threshold, or turn it off, here.`,"show.permissions.title":`Permissions per topic`,"show.permissions.body":`A topic can have its own permission mode: open its menu (⋯) in this tree -> Permissions. Put the topics that read web pages or e-mails in a stricter mode.`,"show.claudeAutoUpdate.title":`Claude Code stays up to date`,"show.claudeAutoUpdate.body":`The server can now update Claude Code by itself to its stable release, only when nothing is running - never in the middle of a turn. Off by default: turn it on with this switch. Each update (or failure) shows in the notifications, the last one here.`};export{e as default};